                        ],
                        "form": "pulverated"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "97dce885-11ac-446c-aa2e-212f4d4cb13b",
                        "entry_id": "3c69b382-18a0-3378-9203-6f9b9fc6b802",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "pulverated"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b02026df-25d4-3830-afcf-776f835f3dd9",
                        "entry_id": "3c69b382-18a0-3378-9203-6f9b9fc6b802",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To beat or reduce to powder or dust; to pulverise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5a0c8a2-8ac9-4303-a326-dade780228fa",
                                "sense_id": "b02026df-25d4-3830-afcf-776f835f3dd9",
                                "text": "Pulverate and mix them with Turpentine; then put them in a glass Alembick, and adde to them Camphyr, and Amber-grise, of each 3 ij."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c81ffd42-b7f5-46e6-9918-ef080803212b",
                                "sense_id": "b02026df-25d4-3830-afcf-776f835f3dd9",
                                "text": "Take of camphora 12 grains, pulverate it with a few drops of spir. vin. rect., add to it sulph. chin. 1 scruple, pulvis doveri 1/2 dram, mix and divide it into 9 doses, write on it: every 2 hours 1 dose."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1eca8df-ce9f-433d-9f13-cd4140344224",
                                "sense_id": "b02026df-25d4-3830-afcf-776f835f3dd9",
                                "text": "It has rendered a service to viatecture which is far better than to pulverate and lift the road into clouds of dust, white-washing our countryside, and making its appearance hideous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "00febf0f-ea1f-4230-8f1c-02a78b542391",
                                "sense_id": "b02026df-25d4-3830-afcf-776f835f3dd9",
                                "text": "\"I've been thinking,” Alix said slowly, “that we fight man's wars and pulverate his garbage and dehydrate his sewerage, but we're not citizens. Why, Manny?\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "341a33a5-7bc8-331a-8e42-89d737ce8182",
                        "entry_id": "3c69b382-18a0-3378-9203-6f9b9fc6b802",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To break up soil or organic matter into a fine, powdery texture, often by means of a special plow."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b842223-9c7e-4130-b0ea-d501151854bf",
                                "sense_id": "341a33a5-7bc8-331a-8e42-89d737ce8182",
                                "text": "Have not we all seen the changed texture and productive quality of a weathered subsoil; seen the sterile clay from the deep drain moulder into manageable and wholesome soil under the culture of a single wintering: reminding us of the saying of Dr. Clarke, that \"the frost is God's plough, which he drives through every inch of ground,\" pulverating and fructifying all ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "538e25b0-2839-48cb-8d9c-6e542fc3ac0f",
                                "sense_id": "341a33a5-7bc8-331a-8e42-89d737ce8182",
                                "text": "[…]shows a field of standing corn stalks being \"pulverated\" into a finished seedbed in one operation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73ba6b27-7c04-4c6f-a79f-485f0f197f39",
                                "sense_id": "341a33a5-7bc8-331a-8e42-89d737ce8182",
                                "text": "Pulverating tough sod — making a finished seedbed, ready for planting, in one operation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ada17a39-35f1-4d18-8fb1-a3a715d3a59f",
                                "sense_id": "341a33a5-7bc8-331a-8e42-89d737ce8182",
                                "text": "Plowing cost less than pulverating."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db165417-eb43-47ca-b16b-81ccf0390763",
                                "sense_id": "341a33a5-7bc8-331a-8e42-89d737ce8182",
                                "text": "Judging from appearances, the plot which had been pulverated (plowed with a pulverator plow on March 17) and drilled immediately and the plot which had been pulverated and disked once were best."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d889c32b-51e7-3562-843d-3926bdb79433",
                        "entry_id": "3c69b382-18a0-3378-9203-6f9b9fc6b802",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To crush or subdue; to overwhelm."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "552a2d4d-ec40-441d-847f-215a50b66a01",
                                "sense_id": "d889c32b-51e7-3562-843d-3926bdb79433",
                                "text": "This subordination of the life to the ideal constitutes the vigorous foundation of his mannish personality. Mousinho's pulverating vocation can be summed up in the following word of immense meaning : «Serving»."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17c8cd6c-2206-48cd-9134-8b1c561b2476",
                                "sense_id": "d889c32b-51e7-3562-843d-3926bdb79433",
                                "text": "Old sleeping bag, cold floor, pulverated heart."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4330521-529a-30a4-b4e2-a87b5066e4f6",
                        "entry_id": "3c69b382-18a0-3378-9203-6f9b9fc6b802",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take a dust bath."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c618560-8152-4f90-9034-3fb98ef4b2d9",
                                "sense_id": "e4330521-529a-30a4-b4e2-a87b5066e4f6",
                                "text": "If the cock be observed to scrape straw together, and rub himself in it, it is no more than what cocks and hens continually do, in heaps of dust, &c., when they have no thought of incubation, but merely from their pulverating instinct."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "27ea9aad-2033-4d2a-bef4-6d5678100a54",
                                "sense_id": "e4330521-529a-30a4-b4e2-a87b5066e4f6",
                                "text": "It is thus we can account for the fact, that whilst these are the most pulverating of birds, continually filling their feathers with dry earth, in order to destroy the vermin which annoy them, those quadrupends similarly roll themselves in the dust, for the sake of ridding themselves of similar enemies picked up in the same situations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "235fc634-18ea-4dc6-8f8c-917db7103202",
                                "sense_id": "e4330521-529a-30a4-b4e2-a87b5066e4f6",
                                "text": "All larks are pulverating birds; but this one is so particularly attached to powdering itself with dust, that, on being supplied with some in a state of captivity, it will immediately testify its joy by a little soft cry, frequently repeated, and by precipitate movements of the wings, and bristling of all the feathers."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c66f08c-3348-3467-bbef-387d9e4de5c0",
                        "entry_id": "3c69b382-18a0-3378-9203-6f9b9fc6b802",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be powdery or granular."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "84ba113c-7c01-4338-946a-d4ae64f3ec09",
                                "sense_id": "0c66f08c-3348-3467-bbef-387d9e4de5c0",
                                "text": "Considerably quantities of pulverating feldspar are found on the rising ground, washed by the rains, near the Guapo mouth and on its left banks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a2e5fd3-c36c-482d-ac19-fe78cbab6580",
                                "sense_id": "0c66f08c-3348-3467-bbef-387d9e4de5c0",
                                "text": "Coppery grey above, uniform or with three or five longitudinal series of blackish dots or elongate quadrangular spots; lower surfaces more or less marbled or pulverated with grey."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e817fdd-50c7-4b49-9dae-5cd468a111ac",
                                "sense_id": "0c66f08c-3348-3467-bbef-387d9e4de5c0",
                                "text": "bluish argillaceious shale with irregularly sandy, friable, or semi-pulverated strata."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
